+5. State the next known milestone, then close briefly.

 ## Use-case writing and performance rules

-- Lead with the newest and most consequential fact.
-- Use absolute dates when timing could be ambiguous.
-- Attribute claims naturally: “According to…”, “The company said…”, “Officials reported…”.
-- Never convert allegations into facts.
-- Do not invent reactions, market moves, motives, or future outcomes.
-- Avoid dramatic prosody for serious events; clarity beats theatricality.
-- If multiple stories are requested, use marks such as `@story_one`, `@story_two`.
